# This is the processing directive for concurrent-reliance-temporal Anchor Modeling in BigQuery
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
#
# BigQuery has no sequences, no unique constraints and no triggers, and its primary and foreign keys are not enforced;
# a dataset is its schema.
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/BigQuery/NamingConvention.js
SQL/BigQuery/derive.js
SQL/BigQuery/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreatePositorAndDefault.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateAttributeAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateAttributeRewinders.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateTieAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateTieRewinders.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/uni/CreateKeys.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/crt/CreateIntegrityChecks.sisula
SQL/BigQuery/AddDescriptions.sisula
